    "turn_text": "So Manu clearly just going very hard after the judge. And again, Democrats, although we know that Democrats are not involved in that trial book, I also want to bring your attention to some other things. I think it's really interesting that Donald Trump chose to hold one of his days outside of the courtroom in New Jersey, a state that we know is not a critical battleground. No hate on New Jersey. I am from here. But his team acknowledges that this isn't really a state that they think can win. However, Donald Trump claimed yesterday that he actually thinks he could be competitive in New Jersey and argue that he's going to make a play for it. He also praised Doug Burgum, the North Dakota governor, also on his VP. contender list. He brought Burgum up to the stage as well and praised him during that. And he said to watch for something big that's coming. It's unclear if that's a tease to him being on his shortlist. But we know from our reporting that Burgum is someone who's very high on his list as a contender for Vice President. Manu.",
