  {
    "episode_id": 96526,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96526.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think it's interesting that one of Donald Trump's chief complaints about these trials is, oh, it's going to take me off of the campaign trail. You know, he's a criminal defendant. He has to be in that courtroom every day that court is in session, but he hasn't really been using his downtime in a way you might say is most effective. He has now been able to sort of take over the news cycle. That's the upside, I guess, of being the criminal defendant is that we're watching everything he does, including whether he is or is not snoozing in the courtroom. He comes out at the end of the day. He makes remarks when he's leaving court. So, you know, there is sort of in a weird way some benefit he gets from being in court, from being in front of cameras every day, even if he's not out there holding rallies.",
