    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and look, the big... Obviously, we're trying to assess and the reason why, of course, is so significant is how does this impact what happens in November? That's a verdict that's going to eventually come. What will that verdict be? Of course, there's no way of predicting how this could play out. But is this the only case that could actually reach a verdict come November? Trump has had success in delaying several of the cases. Has he's done the classified documents case? There's essentially postponed indefinitely because of an order from the judge this past week. The Georgia election subversion case. It says August 5th, but it's unclear if that actually is going to happen before November if it's tied up in other court issues. And as well as the presidential, the election interference case, the federal case, that's paused over the Supreme Court decision about whether he has immunity as he claims that he does. But has he been successful in convincing the American public that he says he's unfairly being prosecuted? Look at the way that this PBS NewsHour poll breaks this down. I mean, between Democrats and Republicans, obviously a major split about whether or not they believe it was fair to see about their thoughts on the investigation, but it was fair, unfair. But independence is split right down the middle. 49-49 about whether they believe Trump is being treated fairly.",
