    "turn_text": "Right, and that's why Democrats aren't necessarily happy that this is dominating the news, as you were talking about. They would love if they controlled the news. It's pretty full of things that they might do. They would love it if the focus this week was on what did he say to donors at mid-marilago about how he'd get rid of regulation if they gave him more money. What are his tax policy? There are classic democratic issues that they beat Mitt Romney with that they think Donald Trump is vulnerable on and they talk about them, feel Biden talks about them, and they can't get covered. I'm not saying that as a helpless person in the media, Trump is also in public talking more about these trials. One thing he does in New Jersey, he said this about Henry Choir when he got indicted last week too in Texas, is that he has a monomyth that everything happening, every political corruption case is the Biden administration trying to take out its enemies. And it's very simple to understand, that's very direct, that positions him as the guy who's fighting corruption, and Democrats are struggling to say, well look at the record he might bring into the White House.",
